From: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:34:37 -0400
Subject: chrome/m156:[M156]Fix potential heap OOB write in SkRgnBuilder for
 conic paths

SkRgnBuilder::init pre-allocates a fixed-size working buffer based on
the path's vertical span and the worst-case number of X-transitions per
scanline (computed by count_path_runtype_values).

Previously, verb_to_max_edges budgeted at most 2 edges for kConic_Verb.
However, SkEdgeBuilder and SkEdgeClipper approximate each conic by
subdividing it into up to 2^kMaxConicToQuadPOW2 (32) quadratics, each of
which can be chopped at its Y-extremum into up to 2 monotonic edges.
When a conic is subdivided near a scanline center, floating-point
rounding across the subdivided quads can cause multiple segments from a
single conic to cross the same scanline, exceeding the pre-allocated
transition budget and writing out-of-bounds in SkRgnBuilder::blitH.

Update verb_to_max_edges to budget 2 << SkConic::kMaxConicToQuadPOW2
(64) edges per conic, and use SkSafeMath when accumulating maxEdges in
count_path_runtype_values to guard against integer overflow.

Bug: 569674218
Fixed: 578796801
Change-Id: Ie8b0bb19e40f042586391e7b1b1f30c939a8f9c4
